It really is. Especially when you realize how many questions you never would have thought to ask until life put you in a position where you couldn’t avoid them.

And then there’s another layer: the questions life makes you ask reveal something about the life you’ve lived.

Two people can experience the same thing and walk away asking completely different questions. One asks, “Why did this happen to me?” Another asks, “What can I do with this?” And someone else asks, “What am I not seeing?”

Sometimes the most important change isn’t finding a better answer. It’s becoming someone capable of asking a better question.

And sometimes you discover that the question you’ve been trying to answer your whole life wasn’t even the right one.

What’s life got you asking this morning?